* TR10 RX_LO_DIV -- CMOS clock buffer, divide-by-2 and 25 % duty generator.
*
* The VCO runs at 2*f_lo.  This block:
*   1. AC-couples and slices the VCO sine into a rail-to-rail clock;
*   2. a master-slave divider of gated NAND latches divides by two.  The
*      master output m and the slave output s are 90 deg apart at f_lo, so
*      they are the I/Q square waves; the toggle feedback is D = s_bar
*      (sampling s would hold instead of toggle);
*   3. four AND gates combine adjacent quadrature phases into the four
*      25 % duty pulses the passive mixer needs.
*
* Ports: clk vdd vss lo0 lo90 lo180 lo270
*   clk   single-ended VCO output, ~1.2 Vpp around 2.5 V (AC coupled here)
*   lo*   0/5 V, 25 % duty, 0/90/180/270 deg
*
* All gates are PDK MOS.  rgval=-1 on every analog MOS.
.subckt INV in out vdd vss
Xp out in vdd vdd PMOS_nf w=20u l=1u nf=2 rgval=-1
Xn out in vss vss NMOS_nf w=10u l=1u nf=2 rgval=-1
.ends INV

.subckt NAND2 a b out vdd vss
Xpa out a vdd vdd PMOS_nf w=20u l=1u nf=2 rgval=-1
Xpb out b vdd vdd PMOS_nf w=20u l=1u nf=2 rgval=-1
Xna out a n1 vss NMOS_nf w=20u l=1u nf=2 rgval=-1
Xnb n1 b vss vss NMOS_nf w=20u l=1u nf=2 rgval=-1
.ends NAND2

.subckt AND2 a b out vdd vss
Xn a b nb vdd vss NAND2
Xi nb out vdd vss INV
.ends AND2

* Gated D latch from NANDs: transparent while en is high.
*   S = NAND(d,en), R = NAND(S,en), q = NAND(S,qb), qb = NAND(R,q)
* NAND2 pin order is (a b out) -- keep the output last.
.subckt LATCH_D d q qb en vdd vss
Xs  d  en ns vdd vss NAND2
Xr  ns en nr vdd vss NAND2
Xq  ns qb q  vdd vss NAND2
Xqb nr q  qb vdd vss NAND2
.ends LATCH_D

.subckt RX_LO_DIV clk vdd vss lo0 lo90 lo180 lo270
* ---- slice the VCO sine into a CMOS clock ------------------------------
Cac clk ck 10n
Rb1 ck vdd 100k
Rb2 ck vss 93k
XI0 ck ckb vdd vss INV
XI1 ckb clk_b vdd vss INV

* ---- master-slave toggle: D = s_bar -----------------------------------
XL1 sb m mb clk_b vdd vss LATCH_D
XL2 m  s sb ckb   vdd vss LATCH_D

* ---- 25 % duty combiner ------------------------------------------------
* phases: I+ = m, I- = mb, Q+ = s, Q- = sb
Xa0 m  s  lo0   vdd vss AND2
Xa1 s  mb lo90  vdd vss AND2
Xa2 mb sb lo180 vdd vss AND2
Xa3 sb m  lo270 vdd vss AND2
.ends RX_LO_DIV
